    title: 'Weight by size, do not average percentages',
    body: 'When several percentages apply to differently-sized groups - margins on different products, growth rates for different regions - the overall figure is weighted by group size, not the simple average of the percentages. The bigger group always pulls the blended figure toward itself. If your answer sits exactly halfway between the two percentages, that is usually a sign you averaged instead of weighted.',
    link: 'page-tips',
