    tag: 'Maths concept',
    title: 'Compute the full total, then subtract exclusions',
    body: 'When a question describes a standard scenario (every pair shakes hands, every team plays every other team) and then adds an exception (a few pairs skip it, two fixtures are cancelled), work out the full unrestricted total first using the standard formula, then subtract the excluded cases afterward. Trying to build the exception into the formula itself is where this usually goes wrong.',
    link: 'page-tips',
