    tag: 'Maths concept',
    title: 'Three unknowns need three full equations',
    body: 'With two unknowns, a quick substitution often gets you there fast. With three, that shortcut stops working - you need three genuinely independent equations and a full elimination process, carried through cleanly to the end. There is no shortcut that skips this; the question is really testing whether you can manage the arithmetic without losing track of a variable.',
    link: 'page-tips',
