    body: 'When a value goes through several rate changes in a row - three discounts stacked on top of each other, a growth rate that compounds every period, two workers whose combined rate changes partway through a job - each new rate applies to wherever the value actually stands at that moment, never back to the original figure. Combine the rates into a single multiplier where you can, and round only once, at the very end - rounding or resetting mid-sequence is where small errors creep in and compound.',
