    body: 'When a value grows from a start figure to an end figure over several periods and you need the steady rate per period, dividing the total growth by the number of periods overstates it, because it ignores compounding. Take the n-th root of the overall growth factor instead - end divided by start, to the power of 1/n, minus 1.',
    link: 'page-tips',
